    through the generated public API.
  - Authorization, user, decision, and rule-info types are module-local and are not assignable to k8s.io/apiserver types.
    cause: compatibility.apiserver: local
    The local mode is an intentional public API break selected by the profile;
    external mode preserves real apiserver identity.
  - ConfirmNoEscalation receives explicit user and namespace arguments instead of reading private apiserver request-context keys.
    cause: compatibility.apiserver: local
    Private context key identity cannot be recreated safely outside
    k8s.io/apiserver, so local mode makes the inputs explicit.
  - k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/apis/rbac.AddToScheme no longer performs its schemeRegistration effect at import time.
